  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILO continues to support the Government of Fiji to apply ratified international labour conventions, and move towards ratification of other instruments including Convention No. 187, 188 and 143. ILO has also supported Fiji to report on the application of a number of Conventions which have not been reported on for a number of years, including Conventions No. 100, 111 and 169. ILO has continuously supported the reform of the Employment Relations Act to meet the recommendations of ILO supervisory bodies. ILO is also providing technical assistance in the area of wages with a view to achieving ratification of Convention 131 and support to Fiji for their reporting in C169 due in September 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
